OL,3,GNEWSABadenoch visits Piddington over
OL,4,AMoD base asylum plan
OL,5,
OL,6,FConservative leader Kemi Badenoch
OL,7,Fvisited villagers who voted to quit the
OL,8,FUK in a symbolic referendum held in
OL,9,Fprotest against plans to house migrants
OL,10,Fon Ministry of Defence (MoD) land.
OL,12,FVillagers in Piddington, near Bicester,
OL,13,Fvoted last Tuesday over Home Office
OL,14,Fproposals to house about 1,300 male
OL,15,Fasylum seekers at MoD Bicester.
OL,17,FBadenoch told reporters the plan was a
OL,18,F"safeguarding issue", with some living
OL,19,Fthere telling her that they worried
OL,20,Fabout their safety.
OL,23,APub: 21-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
